# construction/fleet-roster.kyri -- the fleet's one seat table.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The binding seat -> tree -> engine is the fleet's only real datum, and it
# was spelled in six independent places across two executables: fleet-loop.sh's allow-list, its
# want_tree case, its FLEET_DRY case and its run_lap case, plus fleet_rearm.sh's report_seat rows
# and its relaunch case. Nothing compared them, and by `20260904` two had already drifted -- the
# loop admitted six seat names while the re-arm reported nine, and the elder-name remap seated on
# Keaton's word lived in one file and not the other. A rule written six times is a rule six files
# may quietly come to disagree about; this is that rule written once.
#
# THE SHAPE is the standing roster's own: a record opens with `seat` and carries plain key-value
# lines until the next one. Read it with tools/fixtures/f/fleet_roster_scan.sh rather than by
# grepping here, so one parse serves sh, Rishi, and the launcher prose alike.
#
# STATUS is the field that lets an elder seat stay readable without pretending it runs. `live` is
# a seat the fleet sails today; `parked` is one whose tree no host currently holds, kept by name
# because it may sail again and because an absent directory is a filesystem accident where a
# parked row is a declaration. fleet_rearm.sh already reports an absent tree honestly; this makes
# that honesty something a reader can check against intent.
#
# ELDER names the seat's prior spelling, so a hand who types the old word is corrected rather than
# refused. The word is retired from the seat name, never from the reader's muscle memory.
format fleet-roster-v1

# -- the three Earth ships, names seated 20260904 on Keaton's word ----------------------------
seat incense
tree grain-incense
engine claude
lane law, active-designing, iterative review, and the captain's hat
status live
seated 20260904.013013

seat pheromone
tree grain-pheromone
engine claude
lane the molecular star -- the language details a rune wants
elder furrow
status live
seated 20260904.013013

seat petrichor
tree grain-petrichor
engine claude
lane docs-geode (tend, never rename) and prose-product
elder harvest
status live
seated 20260904.013013

# -- three ships seated `20260904.214754` on Keaton's word, awaiting their trees ---------------------
# STATUS `berthed` is the third word, and it earns its place the way `parked` did: a berthed seat
# has a lane, a prompt, and a name, and no tree yet. `live` would have the re-arm report an absent
# directory as if a ship had gone missing, and `parked` would say it had sailed and stopped. Neither
# is true of a ship being built. `--live` excludes it, so the loop and the recipe stay honest, and
# the tree birth is `rishi/bin/rishi run tools/b/birth_a_clone.rish /home/keeper/grain-<seat>`
# followed by a `claude login` on that host, which is a hand.
seat bakery
tree grain-bakery
engine claude
lane core infrastructure, Lindy-first and crux-first -- and the fleet's own friction
status live
seated 20260904.214754

seat diffuser
tree grain-diffuser
engine claude
lane moonshots and whitepaper research -- toroidal, energy-saving, radial-polar; in tandem with bakery
status live
seated 20260904.214754

seat grass
tree grain-grass
engine claude
lane the four auditing passes -- New Gauge, Civic Style, foundations, TAME Guidance
status live
seated 20260904.214754

# -- COPAL and PATCHOULI, seated 20260905.164639 on Keaton's word. Two more Earth aromas, and
# each takes a module family that stood with real code and no standing guard. The pair was measured
# rather than chosen for symmetry: `mantra/` holds 32 Rye modules and 9,175 lines with 120 files
# outside it reaching in, and `amphora/` holds 10 modules and 3,861 lines -- and on `20260905`
# NEITHER had a single witness on the standing roster. Roughly 13,000 lines of load-bearing Rye
# moved from unguarded to owned by seating these two rows.
#
# The lanes are drawn by TERRITORY rather than by topic, because two ships wanting the same files
# serialize however many cores the pier has. Copal takes the vessels, patchouli takes the core.
#
# ALL EIGHT EARTH SEATS READ `live` FROM `20260905.175234`, when the pier grew to 8 vCPU and 16 GB and
# Keaton asked for eight ships. `status` says whether the fleet sails a seat today, and these five
# are about to be. It also earns each of them a STAGGER SLOT: `fleet-loop.sh` reads its offset from
# the LIVE roster, so a berthed ship would have taken slot 1 alongside incense and never staggered
# at all -- five ships opening their laps in the same second is the one shape the offset exists to
# prevent. The loop itself never read `status`; it checks only that the seat's tree is this tree.
#
# GRASS WAS NOT NARROWED, though a narrowing was proposed in the same breath as these two seats and
# briefly written here. The proposal read grass's one-line lane -- *the four auditing passes* -- and
# called it a collision with every other room. Its stanza governs that already, in two places: it
# says to improve docs-geode *alongside petrichor, whose lane it is -- name a find rather than
# taking it*, and never to convert a file *into another ship's seat without its word*. A lane
# summary is not the charter, and the charter had the discipline the summary could not show.

seat copal
tree grain-copal
engine claude
lane amphora and the resins -- vessels, sealing, and what a record keeps when it is put away
status live
seated 20260905.164639

seat patchouli
tree grain-patchouli
engine claude
lane mantra and tally -- the weave and the bounded core; the base note the rest is built over
status live
seated 20260905.164639

# -- the aether seats, parked. Their charter stays testimony at
# active-designing/20260829-203718_the-six-bodies-and-the-always-fleet.md, and every law it earned
# -- one tree per star, claim-as-override, the ruling seats -- the Earth trio inherits whole.
seat silence
tree grain-silence
engine claude
lane the infrastructure half of Grain in Glow
status parked
seated 20260829.203718

seat hush
tree grain-hush
engine claude
lane Pond completes the enclosure, under the accrete-only boundary
status parked
seated 20260829.203718

seat dream
tree grain-dream
engine codex
lane the systems core -- Caravan, Tally, the Scribe seams
status parked
seated 20260829.203718

# The interactive field sitting. It runs no unattended loop, which is why `engine field` is its
# own word rather than a blank: a seat with no engine would read as a row somebody forgot to
# finish, and this one is finished.
seat sound
tree grain
engine field
lane the interactive bench -- Glow language custody, and where rulings land
status parked
seated 20260829.203718
